mode: "100644"
text: "# SEO workflow, pin checklist + two worked examples\n\n## Keyword research workflow\n1. Start with a **pillar** (one topic at a time). 2. In **Pinterest search**, type the seed term and\nread **autocomplete** + the **guided-search tiles**. 3. Check **Pinterest Trends/Predicts** for\nseasonality + rising terms. 4. Scan **related pins** of top results for the language people use. 5.\nCollect **long-tail, high-intent** phrases (\"budget freelance tax tips\", not \"tax\"). (Cross-check with\n`social-seo`.)\n\n## The pin SEO checklist (every pin)\n- **Title:** keyword + clear benefit (\"5 Freelance Tax Tips to Stop Overpaying\").\n- **Description:** 2–3 natural keyword phrases + context + a CTA (\"Read more\").\n- **Board:** keyword-themed, specific (\"Freelance Finance Tips\").\n- **Alt text + image file name:** keyworded (e.g. `freelance-tax-tips-2026.jpg`).\n- **Link:** the **relevant** page that delivers (not the homepage).\n- **Design:** 2:3 (1000×1500), keyword text overlay, on-brand, scroll-stopping.\n\n## Boards / cluster structure\nPick one pillar → 3–6 keyword-themed boards under it → 3–7 fresh pins/week per board. Keep boards\nunmistakably on-topic (cluster authority). Don't dump 5 pins to one board in a day — **space them.**\n\n## Fresh-design strategy\nFor each blog/product/landing page, make **3–5 distinct pin designs** (different image, layout,\noverlay, angle) and publish them **over time** (≥72h apart for the same URL). Distinct designs = more\nfresh pins = more distribution + more shots at the top 1% that drive most traffic.\n\n## Pin type by goal\n| Goal | Pin type | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Traffic / clicks | Static (links out) | the workhorse |\n| Engagement / reach | Video (9:16, 6–15s) | ~2× engagement; links too |\n| Shopping | Product / Collage / Rich | shoppable |\n\n(Idea Pins are retired — Pinterest unified everything into one Pin format; every pin can carry a link.)\n\n## Worked example 1 — evergreen blog traffic pin (blunt indie-founder voice)\n```\nPILLAR: freelance finance   BOARD: \"Freelance Tax Tips\"\nTITLE: \"The 30% Rule That Saved My Tax Bill\"\nDESC: \"Most freelancers overpay tax. Move 30% of every invoice to a second account the day it lands.\nSimple freelance tax tip that actually works. Read the full breakdown.\"\nDESIGN: 2:3, bold overlay \"THE 30% RULE\", terminal-green accent (via ideogram). FILE: freelance-30-percent-tax-rule.jpg\nLINK: the specific blog post (not homepage). VARIANTS: 4 distinct designs, 72h apart.\n```\n\n## Worked example 2 — seasonal gift-guide pin (warm studio voice)\n```\nPILLAR: gifting   BOARD: \"Gifts for Small-Business Owners\"\nTITLE: \"12 Calm Gifts for the Overworked Founder (2026)\"\nDESC: \"A gentle gift guide for the small-business owner in your life -- practical, calm, and under $50.\nSave for later.\" LAUNCH: 60-75 days before the holiday.\nDESIGN: 2:3 collage-style, soft palette, \"2026 GIFT GUIDE\" overlay. LINK: the gift-guide page.\n```\n\nBoth: keyword-led; 2:3; relevant link (not homepage); brand voice; designs via `ideogram`/`nano-banana`;\nscheduled steadily (72h between same-URL) via `scheduling-and-queue → WoopSocial`; measured in native\nPinterest Analytics. Evergreen ones pair with `content-recycling`; seasonal ones launch early.\n"
